  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1242 PM MDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nThe monsoon high remains in place over western NM on Tuesday where \ntemps will once again threaten records. It will be a tad cooler \nacross the northeast thanks to the passage of a weak backdoor front. \nMoist, upslope flow in the wake of the front will increase the \ncoverage of convection along the central mountain chain and \neventually central NM during the evening hours. The monsoon high \nwill slowly shift off to the northwest mid to late week, allowing \nfor modest moisture increases across central and southern New \nMexico. Storm coverage will trend up slightly, with scattered \ncoverage each afternoon and evening, favoring the high terrain of \nwestern and northern NM. PWATs at KABQ will hold steady right around \nthe seasonal average (~0.9\"), with slightly less moisture across the \nnorthwest where storm coverage will be less. From Wednesday onward, \ntemperatures will drop below record levels, but it will still remain \nhot with temperatures generally 5 to 10 degrees above average.",
